        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Community Counts: Teton High School Booster Club</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/47465.webp" alt="Community Counts: Teton High School Booster Club" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>Dear Tin Cup Donors,</p>

<p>I am writing to let you know how helpful and incredible the Teton High School Booster Club has been this year for the Orchestra Class at THS. </p>

<p>We have been planning to take a trip since September and had made some successful attempts at fundraising to offset the cost so that students would be able to travel to Utah on May 16th.&nbsp; We sold concessions at a basketball game, held Bake Sales, sold tickets to our MidWinter Music Festival Concert, but we just were not getting close to our goal.</p>

<p>I wanted my students to be able to comfortably afford the cultural experience of attending the Utah Symphony and Hale Center Theater, along with a Music Therapy Workshop, the Violin-Making School of America, the Orchestra at Temple Square rehearsal,&nbsp; and some other amazing experiences.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>

<p>I had asked the Booster Club to help fund our tickets to attend the Utah Symphony, not totally sure if they would be able to donate&nbsp; $180.00 to our cause.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>

<p>To my surprise, not only were they willing to do this, but they made an offer of help many times larger than my initial request.&nbsp; I was absolutely humbled and shocked to find out that they would be able to cover almost half of the remaining costs after we had pitched in our fundraising dollars.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>

<p>It was such a relief to know that there was an organization who cares about students, their success, and growth.&nbsp; This organization exists in order to help provide students with opportunities that will build memories for a lifetime.&nbsp; It means so much to me and to the music students of Teton High School.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>

<p><br>I hope that when considering where to put the non-profit money received from the Tin Cup challenge, that the THS Booster Club will be at the top of your list.&nbsp; They are an organization whose resources will be well-spent on the students in our community.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>

<p>Thank you so much for your consideration.</p>

<p>Sincerely,</p>

<p>Julie Schindler</p>

<p>Teton Strings Teacher<br>THS &amp; TMS</p>
